{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>From the east to En.</b> A place-name. And the pass runs along its east — so Ein lies inland of the pass, and it is from the land of Israel." "<b>And the border shall go down.</b> Whenever the border runs from north to south, it is 'going down.'" "<b>And it shall strike against the shoulder of the Sea of Kinneret eastward.</b> That the Sea of Kinneret be within the border, to the west, and the border to the east of the Sea of Kinneret. From there it went down to the Jordan, and the Jordan stretches and comes from north to south at Alachson, slanting toward the east, approaching the side of the land of Canaan opposite the Sea of Kinneret, and stretching along the eastern side of the land of Israel (opposite the Sea of Kinneret) until it falls into the Dead Sea. From there the border terminates at its outlets to the Dead Sea — from which begins the pass at the southeastern corner. Thus it surrounds it on all four sides."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:45.814531344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}